From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dnsapi: Fail instead of calling a Unix side that did not
 load.

dnsapi's Unix side needs libresolv, which the console does not have, so
its __wine_init_unix_call fails and the handle stays 0 ("No libresolv
support, expect problems"). Every later call still went through it, and
the dispatcher read the function table at address 0: a syscall fault on
the caller's thread. iphlpapi's GetAdaptersAddresses asks DnsQueryConfig
for the DNS servers once nsiproxy answers it, and a RE Engine game's
main thread stopped there (measured).

Without the Unix side each call now returns ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, so the
callers see no servers and no search list, as on a machine with none.
---
 dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h b/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h
index d2b57b9..e913a91 100644
--- a/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h
+++ b/dlls/dnsapi/dnsapi.h
@@ -130,4 +130,7 @@ enum unix_funcs
     unix_funcs_count
 };
 
-#define RESOLV_CALL( func, params ) WINE_UNIX_CALL( unix_ ## func, params )
+/* Without the Unix side (its library failed to load) every call fails instead of
+ * calling through a null handle. */
+#define RESOLV_CALL( func, params ) \
+    (__wine_unixlib_handle ? WINE_UNIX_CALL( unix_ ## func, params ) : ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED)
